``pylint`` invoked without any module or package now lints the current working
directory, as if ``pylint .`` had been run, instead of exiting with code 32 and
``No files to lint: exiting.``. The ``files`` option, which now defaults to ``.``,
still sets what to lint from the configuration file. The help is still available
with ``pylint --help`` or ``pylint --long-help``. ``--from-stdin`` still requires
a file name, and now exits with code 32 instead of a traceback when it is missing.
When every message is disabled (``--disable=all``), pylint now prints
``No messages to check: exiting.``.

The ``ignore`` option now skips by default the directories that never hold the code
of a project: version control (``.git``, ``.hg``, ``.svn``, ``.bzr``), virtual
environments (``.venv``, ``venv``, ``.tox``, ``.nox``), build artefacts (``dist``,
``_build``, ``.eggs``, ``buck-out``, ``__pypackages__``, ``node_modules``) and tool
caches (``.mypy_cache``, ``.pytype``, ``.ruff_cache``, ``.direnv``, ``.pants.d``),
the same list as ``ruff``. ``pylint`` in a project root therefore does not lint the
virtual environment. Setting ``ignore`` in a configuration file still replaces the
whole list, so configurations generated by earlier versions keep ``ignore=CVS``.

Closes #5701
